<section class="hero">
  <div class="shell hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Independent security research / Indonesia</span>
      <h1>Every system has <em>a fracture.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">RETAK goes into the dark space between what a system promises and what it actually protects—then returns with reproducible proof.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">Enter the CVE record <span>↗</span></a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="<%= base('/method/') %>">Trace the method</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-footnote"><span>05 public CVEs</span><span>Evidence over theatre</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fracture-stage" aria-label="A glowing natural fissure opening into an abstract abyss">
      <span class="stage-coordinate coordinate-one" aria-hidden="true">06°10′S</span>
      <span class="stage-coordinate coordinate-two" aria-hidden="true">fracture / 05</span>
      <span class="orbit orbit-one" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="orbit orbit-two" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="orbit orbit-three" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="abyss-disc" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="disc-aura"></span>
        <span class="disc-shadow"></span>
        <svg class="hero-crack" viewBox="0 0 600 700" role="presentation">
          <g fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path class="crack-glow" d="M329-10 300 101l18 70-52 79 29 61-70 105 31 76-74 121 19 98"/>
            <path class="crack-core" d="M329-10 300 101l18 70-52 79 29 61-70 105 31 76-74 121 19 98"/>
            <path class="crack-branch" d="m300 101-104-51M318 171l116-83M266 250l-143 22M295 311l132 58M225 416 92 15 77-55M256 492l-129 65M182 613l-91 11M201 711l81-76 99-14"/>
            <path class="crack-hairline" d="m196 50-37 8-42-22m317 52 31 4 28-30M123 272l-43-35-50 7m397 125 54-13 44 27M127 557l-51 43-50 2m356 19 39 30 61-7"/>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <span class="disc-word">RETAK</span>
      </div>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-source">attacker source</span>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-guard">broken assumption</span>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-impact">proven impact</span>
      <div class="stage-record"><small>Current signal</small><strong>Boundary open</strong><span>Edge · Firefox · Safari</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="metric-strip">
  <div class="shell metric-grid">
    <div class="metric-definition"><strong>re·tak</strong><span>/rəˈtak/ · a crack, split, or fracture</span></div>
    <div><strong>05</strong><span>verified fractures</span></div>
    <div><strong>03</strong><span>coordinated vendors</span></div>
    <div><strong>01</strong><span>standard: proof</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section research-section cve-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">The fracture archive</span><h2>Proof left<br><em>in the stone.</em></h2></div>
      <p>Five fixed vulnerabilities across major browser families. No inflated claims—every mark leads to a canonical CVE and vendor advisory.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cve-ledger">
<% @discoveries.each_with_index do |discovery, index| %>
<%= discovery_row(discovery, index: index + 1) %>
<% end %>
    </div>
    <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">Open the canonical CVE archive <span>↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section method-preview">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">The research ritual</span><h2>Follow the <em>fracture.</em></h2></div>
      <p>A precise sequence that separates an interesting code path from a vulnerability worth reporting.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Model the boundary</h3><p>Map actors, data, authority, expected guards, and the security promise under test.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Trace source to sink</h3><p>Use focused LLM-assisted review to connect attacker control to a sensitive operation.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Build the oracle</h3><p>Test the earliest unknown edge with exact artifacts, positive controls, and guarded negatives.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Prove the impact</h3><p>Promote only reproducible, attacker-observable consequences with honest limitations.</p></article>
    </div>
    <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/method/') %>">Read the complete method <span>↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact-band">
  <div class="shell contact-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Open a channel</span><h2>Bring us the boundary.<br><em>We’ll find the crack.</em></h2></div>
    <div><p>Available for authorized security research, source review, and research collaboration.</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:jodyritonga@gmail.com">jodyritonga@gmail.com <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
